{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":227800,"duration_api_ms":229601,"ttft_ms":172421,"ttft_stream_ms":1942,"time_to_request_ms":17,"num_turns":2,"result":"{\"verdict\":\"APPROVE\",\"findings\":[\"A1 [G3/B3 — advisory, routed to the queued record-comment refresh; not blocking]. `docs/ai-template-redesign-2026-09-05-codex/DECOMPOSITION-AMENDMENTS.md` was edited in this sitting (its H5 paragraph now cites the SN-036 owner ruling and the hat-by-hat outcomes), but its closing \\\"Implementation review subject (2026-09-06)\\\" paragraph still says, in the present tense, \\\"TC-211 retains its incomplete normal sample because the applicable SR-161 machine perspective record is absent (the debt already stated in LLR-183)\\\". LLR-183's amended Detail no longer states that debt, and SR-161 no longer imposes a machine record. This is the same class the prior F3 fixed in `inspection-procedures.md`, swept in one file and not the other. It is documentation, not a spine cell, and it sits with the F4 class the owner already routed to a follow-up, so I record it rather than refuse closure: the fix is one tense/marker edit (\\\"the procedure then required … replaced by the 2026-09-06 ruling\\\"), not a re-opening of any row.\",\"A2 [G2/B2 — advisory, no change requested]. Detection asymmetry in the abnormal-input set. Amended SR-161 carries two clauses: the brief presents every applicable perspective's question, and the review record names each outcome. The new \\\"Missing perspective outcome\\\" counterexample demonstrates detection of the second clause; nothing demonstrates detection of the first (a brief that silently omits an applicable hat's question). The Inspection procedure does require confirming the brief presents each question, so the obligation is verifiable, but its discriminating case is asserted rather than exhibited. Worth an added abnormal input at the next revision of the procedure; adding one now would exceed the ruled scope, and I do not treat an unexhibited case as a failure of the amendment.\",\"A3 [G1/G3 — recorded state, not a defect]. Two consequences of this sitting are live and correctly left to their own routes, recorded here so closure cannot be read as absorbing them: (i) TC-178 is an Approved row whose `expected` cell was amended in this change and whose snapshot is not re-seeded; (ii) SN-036, SR-161 and LLR-183 are Approved rows amended in place, and SR-161's `verification` moved Test -> Inspection. Both are snapshot/re-attest drift pending the separate adjudication the prompt names. This record grants no Status approval and no snapshot permission. F4 (stale SN-036 record half in `hats.py`'s docstring and `hats.toml`'s header — both still say the per-decomposition record is \\\"NOT BUILT YET\\\") and F5 (the rubric carries no SN-036 anchor) are confirmed still present and confirmed out of the ruled scope. F6 is settled by the owner's explicit \\\"Rationale names this ruling\\\" instruction, which takes precedence over the standing no-citation-frame convention; the detector advisory stays visible and warn-only.\"],\"basis\":\"IDENTITY AND PROVENANCE (G1). Fresh non-author reviewer: I authored none of the amended rows, the procedure, the dispositions, the prior review or the owner rulings, and I read only the supplied source with tools disabled. Rubric: docs/rubrics/change-review-records.md, digest copied verbatim from this sitting's FILE manifest line — 81a0de90a0d34ae1181cbfe9de083cc22c52d1fb1ac31f8a — with no reconstructed or completed suffix; anchors G1-G5 / B1-B5 as numbered there; intent sources SN-012, SN-024, SN-036, SN-037 read from the supplied needs registry. Model, session and invocation metadata are bound by the launcher record and are not restated. Record path: docs/reviews/2026-09-06-sn036-closure-structured-opus.md.\\n\\nARTIFACT ACCEPTANCE VS REVIEW, AND INSPECTION. This is a review record only. It approves no Status, permits no snapshot, min